From 1d2bd476f6386d6b72480205ec89bb83b1422f20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:35:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Live TV guide: lists kept while nothing is written, first
 screenful first, listings for the rows on screen first

Opening Live TV read the same channel list up to three times (the guide's, and the playing
channel's group twice), every visit read everything again, and every list shown asked for 40
channels' listings twice. Now:

- LiveDb counts its list and guide writes; LivePage keeps the lists it read (ScopeLists) and
  shows a list again without reading it while nothing was written since. A visit with nothing
  changed reads the playlists and groups only, and the guide's listings stay as loaded.
- The guide's own list is read before the playing channel's group, which shares its copy.
- A list no longer wanted stops being read (CancellationSignal), so a group looked at next
  doesn't wait behind a long list.
- Of a long list (All channels, All playlists) the first screenful shows at once through the
  position index, the whole list arriving under it without anything moving on screen.
- Listings: the rows on screen are read and shown first, the rows around after; of asks made
  while a key is held only the newest is read.
- Favorites are read from the stars to their channels (it looked every channel up among the
  stars); a playlist's and a group's id are kept once per list, not once per channel.
- The guide isn't drawn again for every word from the player, nor the controls worked out
  again for every logo that lands.
- FirePlayerLive: "groups listed", "first channels shown", "guide listed (... read/kept)",
  "programmes shown", each with its time after opening.

