From b17b304c2cb35be564e811d301523e99ce3d055e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:48:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Live TV: logos kept on disk, a pause the player makes
 itself is shown, the controls set only on news

- Channel logos were downloaded again every time they left the 6 MB memory cache (each scroll
  back, each start of the app). A fetched logo is now kept on disk as decoded (cache folder,
  24 MB, two weeks before its server is asked again, the old copy standing in if it doesn't
  answer); the disk is read on its own thread so a slow logo server doesn't hold those up.
  FirePlayerLive "logos shown (n kept on disk, n fetched, n without one)" after opening.
- The player pauses itself when the sound's output goes away (TV or sound bar switched off or
  over, headphones gone). Only a loss of audio focus was shown as a pause: this one left a
  still picture that said it was playing, and a first Play/Pause press that did nothing.
- The full-screen controls' pods were set again (and the screen laid out again) with every
  word from the player; now only when the status, the pods shown or the playlist changed.
- The channel timing line also says when the tracks were known and how long the picture's
  decoder took to start, so a slow channel change can be read on the TV.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CeAGQc19KZMJTFxzJrjwSq
